In concept-glossary.tex the entry "closed" writes \seeterm\term{close}.
\seeterm takes the term as its argument and wraps it in \term itself
(setup-document.tex:396), so the extra \term nests one in the other and the
reference text is the control sequence \term. Pass the argument alone.
--- concept-glossary.tex
+++ concept-glossary.tex
@@ -842,1 +842,1 @@
-  having been \term{closed} (\seeterm\term{close}).
+  having been \term{closed} (\seeterm{close}).
